On Mon, 1 Jul 2002, Stanislaw Findeisen wrote:

> Hi, I'm _really_ new to the field, and need some _comprehensive_
> documentation about things like:
>
> - basic existing registers and their purposes,
>
> - assembler instructions and their _exact_ semantics
> (like 'call', 'ret' and so on).
>
> Could anyone help?

Get a (paper) book on general x86 assembly programming,
perhaps in your native language. Among online resources,
"Art of Assembly" by R.Hyde is a good start,

> I tried to find sth at linuxassembly.org, but all man can get there
> is fifty tutorials about "hello world" and syscalls...
> I don't want samples, just documentation!  :-)

Should you be more accurate, you'll notice references to several books
and CPU manuals -- this is what you need.

--=20
